cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the article in preferred-citation. To refer to a specific code version, cite the software DOI."
title: "AgroYachay: An open-source IoT and large-language-model platform supporting agronomic and economic decision-making for Andean smallholders"
abstract: "AgroYachay (yachay, 'knowledge' in Quechua) turns low-cost ESP32 telemetry into agronomic and economic decisions for Andean smallholders: real-time monitoring with alerts, pest and disease triage with a locally hosted vision model, conversational agronomy, a computed agricultural almanac, and transparent yield and revenue estimation, in a Spanish, English, Quechua and Aymara interface. Version 3.0.0 is a rewrite of the platform (Rust API, Next.js web application, PostgreSQL, local open models served through an OpenAI-compatible server such as llama.cpp or Ollama). The version described in SoftwareX 36 (2026) 103037 is v1.0.1, archived at Zenodo (doi:10.5281/zenodo.20829992). Version 2 was an internal prototype and was not released."
